# GTM contracts: render, then commit and push (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-17):

> **Always render DOCX and PDF, then commit and push as part of
> every command.**

## The rule

> **When editing `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/contracts/`
> or the contract renderer, the same command that changes markdown
> MUST (1) render every affected variant to Word (`.docx`) and
> Portable Document Format (PDF) via `render-contract.py` /
> `Render-Contract.ps1`, (2) refresh family-folder copies next to
> the markdown, (3) commit explicit paths only, and (4) push
> `origin/main`. Do not leave contract markdown without matching
> Word and PDF. Do not stop at markdown.**

## When it applies

Any edit to templates, YAML defaults, family-folder Word/PDF,
`generating-docx-and-pdf.md`, or
`operator-workflows/scripts/contracts/render-contract.py` /
`Render-Contract.ps1`.

## Required sequence

1. **Render** every affected variant (`msp`, `eula`, `reseller`,
   `psp`, `alliance`, `oem`, `nda`, `reseller-nda`, `alliance-nda`
   when the pack or renderer changed). `$LASTEXITCODE` must be 0.
   Do not pass `--docx-only` unless the operator named it.
2. **Copy** `generated/<stem>-filled.docx` and `.pdf` over the
   family-folder files next to the `.md` (and the NDA copies under
   `nda/` plus any sibling family-folder NDA copies). `generated/`
   stays gitignored.
3. **Commit** explicit paths only. Never `git add -A` /
   `git add .` ([`shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc`](shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc)).
   Temp-file `git commit -F` per
   [`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc).
4. **Push** `origin/main`. Primary `main` only. No worktree. No
   force-push. No `--no-verify`.

Repos: `pam-platform-docs` for papers and family copies;
`operator-workflows` if the renderer changed; `core-assets` if
this rule changed. How-to:
[`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/contracts/generating-docx-and-pdf.md`](../../pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/contracts/generating-docx-and-pdf.md).

## Forbidden

- Reporting a contract edit done with markdown only
- Leaving family-folder Word/PDF stale versus the markdown
- Committing `generated/*-filled.*` (gitignored)
- `git add -A`, force-push, `--no-verify`, extra worktrees

## Required agent behavior

1. Render and refresh copies before the commit of that command.
2. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same
   change set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).
3. Return hashes, file counts, page table, and a Founding grep
   count of 0 in `contracts/` when that cleanup is in scope.

## Origin

2026-09-17 - operator standing command: always render Word and
PDF, then commit and push, as part of every GTM contract command.
